  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The given points (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6) makes 360<sup>o</sup> angle at ‘O’. Hence angle made by vertices 1 and 2 with ‘O’ is 60<sup>o</sup>.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/190774s.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 319px; height: 226px;\" /></p><p>Direction of magnetic field at ‘O’ due to each segment is same. Since it is symmetric star shape, magnitude will also be same.</p><p>Magnetic field due to section BC.</p><p><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>60°</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>30°</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>×</mo><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
